WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.425 --> 00:00:03.308
Unit four. Substance Abuse Prevention!

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.512
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:10.549
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:14.401
Today we learn about Substance Abuse Prevention. Let's go!

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.040
Tobacco. Say it with me. Tobacco!

6
00:00:22.544 --> 00:00:26.010
Alcohol. Say it with me. Alcohol!

7
00:00:29.544 --> 00:00:33.011
Peer pressure. Say it with me. Peer pressure!

8
00:00:36.519 --> 00:00:40.319
Refuse. Say it with me. Refuse!

9
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:46.894
Risk. Say it with me. Risk!

10
00:00:50.381 --> 00:00:53.898
Addiction. Say it with me. Addiction!

11
00:00:57.339 --> 00:01:01.289
Consequence. Say it with me. Consequence!

12
00:01:04.824 --> 00:01:07.991
Decision. Say it with me. Decision!

13
00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:22.383
Tobacco and alcohol can seriously harm a young, growing body. Learning to refuse under peer pressure protects against risk and future addiction. Every decision has a consequence, so it helps to think ahead.

14
00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:25.135
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:31.411
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:31.461 --> 00:01:32.611
Peer pressure!

17
00:01:33.768 --> 00:01:38.870
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:40.074
Consequence!

19
00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:48.679
Did you know? The teenage brain is still developing, which is one reason substances can affect it more strongly than an adult brain.

20
00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:50.367
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:51.064 --> 00:01:58.587
Think and answer. What is one way to say no to peer pressure?

22
00:01:58.637 --> 00:01:59.787
Great answer!

23
00:02:00.835 --> 00:02:05.272
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:05.322 --> 00:02:07.797
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

